To draw a chessboard in LaTeX using FEN notation, you can use the `chessboard` package. Here's an example code:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{chessboard}

% Set up the chessboard
\setmainfont{Arial} % Change font to your preference
\setchessboard{width=8cm, position=center}

% Define the FEN notation
\def\myfen{r2r3r1r1r1r1r1r1r1w1w2w2w2w2w2w2w2}

% Draw the chessboard
\begin{document}
\chessboard[fen=\myfen]
\end{document}
```

This code will produce a 8cm wide chessboard with the given FEN notation. You can modify the `width` and `position` options to adjust the size and position of the chessboard. Also, you can change the font using the `\setmainfont` command.
